      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-38397a5e1e8d",
          "exact": "KISS (\"Keep it simple, stupid\") is a design principle first noted by the U.S. Navy in 1960. First seen partly in American English by at least 1938, KISS implies that simplicity should be a design goal."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-38397a5e1e8d",
          "subject": "KISS (\"Keep it simple, stupid\")",
          "predicate": "is a design principle first noted by the U.S. Navy in 1960",
          "object": "stating that simplicity should be a design goal; the phrase was also seen in American English by at least 1938"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001"
      ],
      "rationale": "claim 三要素在引文中均有对应。第一句 [0,91) 明示 \"KISS ... is a design principle first noted by the U.S. Navy in 1960\"，支持 claim 的\"设计原则\"与\"1960 年由美国海军首次提出\"（\"noted\"与\"提出\"在语境中等价，均为\"首次被美国海军记录/提及\"）；末句 [148,201) \"KISS implies that simplicity should be a design goal\" 直接支持\"简单性应当成为设计目标\"。引文中 [92,146) 的 1938 年英文先例（\"First seen partly in American English by at least 1938\"）补充说明该短语更早出现于美式英语，但所指的是短语本身被使用的时间，与\"美国海军 1960 年首次注意到\"并非同一命题，不构成对 claim 的否定或冲突，故判定为完全支持。注：本请求未提供完整源文本，start/end 以所附引文字符串为参照系计算（引文全长 201 个 Unicode code points，恰为 [0,201) 整段；偏移在源文本中的绝对位置无法进一步核实）。",
